<title>SINGAPORE: TAIWAN TENDERS TO BUY 76,000/T OCTOBER FUEL OIL.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN TENDERS TO BUY 76,000/T OCTOBER FUEL OIL.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy two 38,000 tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent sulphur fuel oil for delivery in October, a CPC source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender seeks one low pour cargo of up 424-centistoke (cst) fuel oil for delivery from October 1-20 and one high pour of up 638-cst for delivery from October 1-30.</p>
<p>The tender closes on August 20 and offers will be valid for two days. Offers are to be on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Keelung, Taichung or Shenao.  </p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought two 0.5-percent sulphur low pour and one 1.0-percent low pour cargoes at around $128.00 and $124.00 per tonne, respectively, on a c-and-f basis.</p>
